          "line": 274,
          "title": "PRTitleQuoted duplicates the existing shellQuote escaping helper",
          "detail": "internal/cli/archive.go:354 already has shellQuote(s string) string { return \"'\" + strings.ReplaceAll(s, \"'\", `'\\''`) + \"'\" } for the identical purpose — escaping a string for a POSIX single-quoted word inside an instruction a session runs verbatim through a shell (used there for `git clean -fd -- \u003cpath\u003e`). PRTitleQuoted re-implements the same close-escape-reopen algorithm (minus the surrounding quotes, left to the template) in a different package instead of factoring one shared helper, so the same shell-quoting rule now lives in two places that could drift independently.",
          "lenses": [
            "consistency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "severity": "minor",
          "file": "internal/cli/cmd_next.go",
          "line": 577,
          "title": "dispatchAgent's hoisted ensureSliceDiff call has no test proving it runs once",
          "detail": "Task 12(F) hoists r.ensureSliceDiff(ctx) out of the reviewer's render closure in dispatchAgent so the slice diff isn't recomputed on every render (the same #51 problem TestWriteStableBriefRendersOnce pins for writeStableBrief). No comparable test counts ensureSliceDiff invocations or diff-file writes for a reviewer dispatch, so a regression that put the call back inside the closure (or dropped the hoist) would not be caught by any test — it would only cost extra idempotent writes, but the fix itself is otherwise unverified.",
          "lenses": [
            "tests"
          ]
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "internal/cli/cmd_next.go",
          "line": 779,
          "title": "dispatchLenses reimplements the writeDispatchBrief helper it should call",
          "detail": "Task 12 introduces r.writeDispatchBrief(dest, render) (lines 639-650) precisely to pair renderFresh with writeStableBriefAt once (#51). dispatchLenses's per-lens loop (lines 772-785) inlines exactly that sequence — text, _, rerr := renderFresh(lensBrief); ...; writeStableBriefAt(p, text, lensBrief) — instead of calling r.writeDispatchBrief(p, lensBrief), which would do the same thing since dest (p) is always non-empty here. The new helper is used at one of its two natural call sites and duplicated at the other, within the same task's own diff.",
          "lenses": [
            "consistency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "internal/cli/cmd_next.go",
          "line": 1017,
          "title": "preparePushPR's own ReadGoals error-wrap is never actually exercised by any test",
          "detail": "preparePushPR (cmd_next.go:1008-1020) calls finish.ReadGoals(r.bdir) a second time and wraps any error as fmt.Errorf(\"%s: %w\", finish.GoalsPath(r.bdir), err) — the behaviour task 12 calls out explicitly (\"an unreadable record is a failure, not not assessed\"). But finish.ReadGoals(bdir) for the same finish/goals.json is already called earlier in the same `next` invocation by goalFacts (internal/cli/finish_facts.go:185-189), from gatherFinishFacts, from gatherFacts, from loop() (cmd_next.go:237-240) — and loop() returns fail() and never reaches decide.Decide/run() if that first call errors. So the malformed-JSON case in TestPushPRBodyListsGoalVerdicts (internal/cli/finish_test.go:661-665, asserting only exit 1 and stderr containing \"JSON\") is satisfied by goalFacts's earlier, unrelated failure — preparePushPR's own error branch at cmd_next.go:1017-1020 is never reached by this test. Deleting that whole `if err != nil { return fmt.Errorf(...) }` check (e.g. replacing with `rec, _ := finish.ReadGoals(r.bdir)`) would not fail any existing test, since for every scenario the tests exercise ReadGoals either succeeds or the run already stopped earlier. The test comment even acknowledges the ambiguity (\"Either way the run stops\") but the assertion doesn't distinguish which code path produced the failure, so it doesn't actually pin the new code.",
          "lenses": [
            "tests"
          ]
        },
        {
          "severity": "minor",
          "file": "internal/cli/cmd_next.go",
          "line": 1042,
          "title": "prGoals's goals.Parse error path is untested",
          "detail": "prGoals (cmd_next.go:1042) reads goals.md and requires goals.Parse to succeed, returning a wrapped error naming the file on failure. TestPushPRBodyListsGoalVerdicts (internal/cli/finish_test.go) only exercises the missing-file branch (os.ReadFile error, by renaming goals.md away); it never writes a syntactically-invalid goals.md to exercise the goals.Parse failure branch and its error-wrapping.",
          "lenses": [
            "tests"
          ]
        }
